## 3. UI behavior: win amounts over matched symbols

**Evidence from `moon_princess_files` CSS** — dedicated classes for **on-screen paytable-style overlays** (count + amount + currency), styled for visibility over the grid:

```1362:1405:C:/Users/valtt/OneDrive/Godot/AXEL/axel_project/exports/moon_princess_files/mobile_videoslot.css
.onscreensymbol_paytable_number
{
    color: #FFF;
    font-size: 22px;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: NeutonBold, Helvetica, Tahoma, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif;
}

.onscreensymbol_paytable_amount
{
    color: #ff0;
    font-size: 22px;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: NeutonBold, Helvetica, Tahoma, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif;
}

.onscreensymbol_paytable_currency_info
{
    color: #ff0;
    font-size: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: NeutonBold, Helvetica, Tahoma, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif;
}

.onscreensymbol_paytable_text_left
{
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 16px;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: NeutonBold, Helvetica, Tahoma, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif;
}

.onscreensymbol_paytable_text_right
{
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 16px;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-family: NeutonBold, Helvetica, Tahoma, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif;
}
```

Interpretation: the shipped UI separates **symbol count** (white), **win amount** (yellow), optional **currency**, and **left/right caption text** — typical for floating win callouts on clusters. **Implementation logic** (when/how amounts attach to symbols) lives inside the minified bundle, not in readable CSS/JS in this export.

---

## Files **not** carrying payout/bet data here

- `C:/Users/valtt/OneDrive/Godot/AXEL/axel_project/exports/game_data.json` — unrelated narrative game metadata.
- `main.js` in `moon_princess_files` — game **history** UI (bet/win columns), not slot math.

---

**Bottom line:** **Bet ladder amounts** appear only as the **partial five-value strip + BET label** in `Screenshot 2026-04-28 145634.png`; the **PDF** confirms five buttons / ± steps but **no EUR list**. **Symbol payout tables** are best documented in **`145838`, `145844`, `145829` PNGs** (and rule text / RTP / clear-grid math in the **PDF**). **`mobile_videoslot.css`** documents **overlay styling** for per-symbol win presentation via `.onscreensymbol_paytable_*`.

